          %p
            Under the further embedding
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi SO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(2)\hookrightarrow SO(3)
            the cyclic and dihedral groups are precisely those
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+subgroups+of+SO%283%29"} finite subgroups of SO(3)
            that, among their
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE+classification"} ADE classification
          #NotationConvention.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              %strong Warning on notation
            %p There are two different conventions for numbering the dihedral groups.
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  The above is the
                  %em algebraic convention
                  in which the suffix gives the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/order"} order
                  of the group:
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %msub
                              %mi D
                              %mrow
                                %mn 2
                                %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mo =
                          %mn 2
                          %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert D_{2 n}\vert} = 2 n
              %li
                %p
                  In the
                  %em geometric convention
                  one writes “
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi D
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_n
                  ” instead of “
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi D
                          %mrow
                            %mn 2
                            %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_{2n}
                  ”, recording rather the geometric nature of the object of which it is the symmetry group.
                %p
                  Furthermore beware that there is yet another group commonly denoted “
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi D
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_n
                  ”, cf. at
                  = succeed "." do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Coxeter+group"} Coxeter group
          %h3#BinaryDihedralGroup Binary dihedral/dicyclic groups
          %p
            Under the further lift through the
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+group"} spin group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+cover"} double cover
            map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi SO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(2) \simeq Spin(3) \to SO(3)
            of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+orthogonal+group"} special orthogonal group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_{2n}
            is covered by the
            = succeed "," do
              %em binary dihedral group
            %em dicyclic group
            and denoted
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi Dic
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  2 D_{2n} = Dic_n
          %p
            Equivalently, this is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lift"} lift
            of the dihedral group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_{2n}
            (
            %a{:href => "#DihedralGroups"}> above
            ) through the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pin+group"} pin group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+cover"} double cover
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+group"} orthogonal group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/O%282%29"} O(2)
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pin%282%29"} Pin(2)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mn 2
                          %msub
                            %mi D
                            %mrow
                              %mn 2
                              %mi n
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ↪
                            %mphantom
                              %mi AA
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Pin
                            %mo −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ↪
                            %mphantom
                              %mi AA
                        %mtd
                          %mi Spin
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 3
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi pb
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi pb
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi D
                            %mrow
                              %mn 2
                              %mi n
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ↪
                            %mphantom
                              %mi AA
                        %mtd
                          %mi O
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ↪
                            %mphantom
                              %mi AA
                        %mtd
                          %mi SO
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 3
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  2 D_{2n}
                  \&amp;\overset{\phantom{AA}}{\hookrightarrow}&amp;
                  Pin_-(2)
                  \&amp;\overset{\phantom{AA}}{\hookrightarrow}&amp;
                  Spin(3)
                  \\\
                  \\big\downarrow
                  \&amp;{}^{(pb)}&amp;
                  \\big\downarrow
                  \&amp;{}^{(pb)}&amp;
                  \\big\downarrow
                  \\\
                  D_{2n}
                  \&amp;\overset{\phantom{AA}}{\hookrightarrow}&amp;
                  O(2)
                  \&amp;\overset{\phantom{AA}}{\hookrightarrow}&amp;
                  SO(3)
                  }
          %p
            Explicity, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℍ
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} j
                  %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{H} \simeq \mathbb{C} \oplus \mathrm{j} \mathbb{C}
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternions"} quaternions
            realized as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cayley-Dickson+double"} Cayley-Dickson double
            of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi ℍ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  SO(2) \simeq S\big( \mathbb{C}\big) \hookrightarrow \mathbb{H}
          %p
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+circle"} unit circle
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi ℍ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C} \hookrightarrow \mathbb{H}
            this way, with group structure given by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiplication"} multiplication
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternions"} quaternions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pin+group"} Pin group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pin%282%29"} Pin(2)
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+of+units"} group of units
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℍ
                    %mo ×
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{H}^\times
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternions"} quaternions
            which consists of this copy of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SO%282%29"} SO(2)
            together with the multiples of the imaginary quaternion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{j}
            with this copy:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Pin
                    %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∪
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} j
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℍ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Pin_-(2)
                  \\;\simeq\;
                  S\big( \mathbb{C}\big)
                  \\;\cup\;
                  \\mathrm{j} \cdot S\big( \mathbb{C}\big)
                  \\;\subset\;
                  S(\mathbb{H})
                  \\;\simeq\;
                  Spin(3)
                  \\,.
          %p
            The binary dihedral group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 D_{2n}
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
            of that generated from
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ≔
                      %mi exp
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mi π
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} i
                        %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                          %mfrac
                            %mn 1
                            %mi n
                        %mo )
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msub
                        %mi Pin
                        %mo −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi Spin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 3
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \coloneqq \exp\left( \pi \mathrm{i} \tfrac{1}{n} \right) \in S(\mathbb{C}) \subset Pin_-(2) \subset Spin(3)
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ≔
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} j
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi Pin
                        %mo −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi Spin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 3
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \coloneqq  \mathrm{j} \in Pin_-(2) \subset Spin(3)
                \.
          %p It is manifest that these two generators satisfy the relations
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi a
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                  %mphantom
                    %mi AA
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi a
                    %mi n
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                  %mphantom
                    %mi AA
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi a
                  %mi x
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi a
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  a^{2n} = 1
                  \\,,
                  \\phantom{AA}
                  x^2 = a^n \; (= -1)
                  \\,,
                  \\phantom{AA}
                  x^{-1} a x = a^{-1}
          %p
            and in fact these
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generators+and+relations"} generators and relations
            fully determine
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 D_{2n}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
