          %h3#group_presentation Group presentation
          %p
            The dihedral group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_{2n}
            has a group presentation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi y
                    %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi xy
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle x,y : x^n=y^2=(xy)^2=1\rangle.
          %p
            From this it is easy to see that it is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-direct+product"} semi-direct product
            of the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_n
            generated by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            and the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_2
            generated by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            is given by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi y
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,^y x= x^{-1}
          %p
            It is a standard example considered in elementary
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+group+theory"} combinatorial group theory
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#quaternion_group__and_triality
            Quaternion group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Q
                    %mn 8
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_8
            and triality
          %div{:style => "float:right;margin:0 10px 10px 0;"}
            %img{:src => "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/59/Dynkin_diagram_D4.png", :width => "100"}/
          %p
            The first binary dihedral group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 D_4
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternion+group"} quaternion group
            of order 8:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi Dic
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi Q
                    %mn 8
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  2 D_4 (= Dic_2) \simeq Q_8
                  \\,.
          %p
            In the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE-classification"} ADE-classification
            this is the entry
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D4"} D4
